# Cartelería de seguridad, memorandos y tablero de fichas de Anima Consolidated (Inglés — idioma fuente canónico)

# Carteles de seguridad SIGN-01..SIGN-10 (20)
sign-01-title = SIGN-01 — Brass Tally Control
sign-01-body = NO BRASS TALLY, NO CAGE DESCENT. TAKE YOUR NUMBER BEFORE YOU DROP.
sign-02-title = SIGN-02 — Anti-Offering Notice
sign-02-body = ORE BELONGS IN THE BUCKET, NOT THE FISSURE. "OFFERINGS" WILL BE DEDUCTED FROM WAGES.
sign-03-title = SIGN-03 — Acoustic Hazard / The Whistlers
sign-03-body = WHEN THE SEAM WHISTLES, CLEAR THE DRIFT. DO NOT ANSWER THE WHISTLERS.
sign-04-title = SIGN-04 — Seismograph & Blasting Limit
sign-04-body = WATCH THE SEISMOGRAPH NEEDLE. NEVER BLAST ABOVE "BREATHE".
sign-05-title = SIGN-05 — Bucket Line Clearance
sign-05-body = KEEP HANDS CLEAR OF THE BUCKET LINE. THE CHAIN STOPS FOR NO MAN.
sign-06-title = SIGN-06 — Geophone Listening Posts
sign-06-body = QUIET WITHIN TEN PACES OF GEOPHONE STAKES. LET THE LISTENER WORK.
sign-07-title = SIGN-07 — High-Tension Conduit Hazard
sign-07-body = WET ROCK CARRIES CURRENT. KEEP PICKS CLEAR OF LIVE CONDUITS.
sign-08-title = SIGN-08 — Thermal Pocket & Lava Warning
sign-08-body = RED SEAM MEANS MOLTEN ROCK. SEAL THE BOREHOLE AND FALL BACK.
sign-09-title = SIGN-09 — Drift Closure Warning
sign-09-body = TRUST THE SURVEY STAKE, NOT YOUR MEMORY. REPORT MOVING WALLS AT ONCE.
sign-10-title = SIGN-10 — Company Rule 44: The Sleeper
sign-10-body = ROCK DOES NOT SLEEP AND CANNOT WAKE. IDLE TALK OF "THE SLEEPER" IS GROUNDS FOR DISMISSAL.

# Memorandos internos MEMO-01..MEMO-06 (13)
memo-header-company = ANIMA CONSOLIDATED — INTERNAL MEMORANDUM
memo-01-subject = MEMO-01 (Oct 12, 1928) — Rhythmic Sub-400m Acoustic Anomaly
memo-01-body = From Lukas Bergmann (Brass Tally #6, Chief Geophone Operator) to Arthur Vance (Chief Surface Engineer): Every geophone stake driven below the -400m level registers the same low-frequency cadence—0.4 cycles per minute in nocturnal rest, rising to fourteen beats per minute whenever a drill bit strikes a rich vein. It is neither the sump pumps nor tectonic settling; when Mateo Aller (Tally #14) halts the bucket line at shift change, the pulse grows clearer. Valentín Condori (Tally #10) and the Bolivian drillers have taken to calling it "the Sleeper." I request permission to install a continuous-drum seismograph at Sub-Station 4. — Margin note by A. Vance: Approved for the drum, Bergmann. Keep the crew's superstitions out of the logbook. Gas pockets throb; granite does not sleep.
memo-02-subject = MEMO-02 (Jun 19, 1929) — Unaccounted High-Grade Ore & "Offerings"
memo-02-body = From Eleanor Sterling (Director of Regional Operations) to Arthur Vance (Chief Surface Engineer) and Thomas Trevithick (Brass Tally #1, Night-Shift Foreman): Accounting reports a 4.2% discrepancy between blasted face estimates and the ore delivered by the bucket line. Foremen confess that crews across all twelve nationalities are tossing raw gold nuggets into deep floor fissures whenever the seismograph needle twitches. Trevithick tells me the men call this an "Offering" and swear the tremors subside within thirty seconds of the drop. Let me be crystal clear: feeding Company gold to a crack in the floor is theft. Bolt SIGN-02 at every chute and dock the wages of any man caught calming the rock with our balance sheet.
memo-03-subject = MEMO-03 (Apr 4, 1930) — Drift Reconfiguration & Pre-Collapse Whistling (Level -580m)
memo-03-body = From Thomas Trevithick (Brass Tally #1) and Valentín Condori (Brass Tally #10) to Arthur Vance (Chief Surface Engineer): Cross-cut 9, which we stripped bare and timbered last Tuesday, was found sealed solid this morning after the midnight settling. We drove a test bore into the new wall expecting rubble and struck solid, unfractured quartz laced with a fresh ribbon of native gold—except the timber frames we left inside were crushed flat and warm to the touch. Worse, three minutes before a roof slab drops, the micro-fissures emit a two-tone harmonic shriek the men call "the Whistlers." If a crew hears the Whistlers and does not sprint, the drift closes over them like a jaw.
memo-04-subject = MEMO-04 (Nov 28, 1930) — Seismograph Thresholds & Mechanical Excitation
memo-04-body = From Arthur Vance (Chief Surface Engineer) to Eleanor Sterling (Director of Regional Operations): By cross-referencing Bridget Gallagher's (Brass Tally #29) powder magazine ledgers with Mateo Aller's (Tally #14) bucket line tachometer and Lukas Bergmann's (Tally #6) geophone traces, the pattern is undeniable. Mount Anima reacts to cumulative acoustic energy across four distinct seismograph thresholds: 1. STIR (25%): First tremors and rockfalls warned by "the Whistlers"; geophones record a 22 bpm pulse. 2. BREATHE (50%): Warm air exhales from faults; old drifts seal while deep Mother Lode cavities dilate. 3. RESTLESS (75%): Pressurized lava pockets rupture; drifts open or seal across levels. 4. WAKE (100%): Projected 90-second total contraction exposing the Heart surrounded by rising lava. Paradoxically, the miners' "Offerings" work: dropping raw gold into active fissures reduces the seismograph reading by roughly 5 percentage points within one minute.
memo-05-subject = MEMO-05 (Oct 17, 1931) — Controlled Agitation Protocol ("Mother Lode" Yield)
memo-05-body = From Eleanor Sterling (Director of Regional Operations) to Arthur Vance (Chief Surface Engineer): The Wall Street credit freeze leaves us no margin for timid mining. Your November study proves that whenever the seismograph crosses the 50% threshold (BREATHE), the mountain's dilation exposes virgin chambers of solid bullion—what Trevithick's men call a Mother Lode. Effective tonight, you will instruct Mateo Aller (#14) to run the bucket line ungreased and have Bridget Gallagher (#29) issue double percussion caps to the drillers. Keep the needle pinned between BREATHE and RESTLESS. Do not inform the shift why the acoustic dampeners have been removed. Let the Sleeper turn over in its bed if it spills gold into our chutes.
memo-06-subject = MEMO-06 (Nov 14, 1931) — Immediate Night-Shift Descent to Thermal Anomaly ("The Heart")
memo-06-body = From Eleanor Sterling and Arthur Vance (Surface Command) to Thomas Trevithick (Tally #1), Bridget Gallagher (Tally #29), and Mateo Aller (Tally #14): Lukas Bergmann (Tally #6) reports that the deep thermal cavity at -620m—designated The Heart—is pulsing beneath the largest potential Mother Lode ever recorded. All 41 brass tallies of the international night shift will descend at 10:00 PM to the -620m level with extra nitroglycerin crates from Gallagher's magazine to force the fault past STIR and BREATHE. Aller will lock the bucket line at maximum haul speed. No crew is permitted to drop a single ounce as an Offering; we need every ton on the surface before dawn to satisfy the bank auditors. If the needle touches WAKE, blast the chamber roof and ride the bucket chain out.

